Project Abstract

Students must select a dataset that aligns with their chosen project topic (e.g., healthcare,
finance, retail, environment, social media, education). The abstract (150–200 words) should
clearly describe the project motivation, the problem to be solved, and the expected
outcomes. It should also explain why the chosen dataset is suitable for the project and what
impact the project could have.

NOTE: Include links to all the datasets you use in the project.

Team Contributions
Each team member must actively contribute to the project. Contributions can include:
- Dataset research and justification.
- Data cleaning and preprocessing.
- Writing analysis code and producing visualizations.
- Managing GitHub workflow (branches, commits, merges).
- Building the Streamlit application.
- Writing documentation and project report.
Team roles and individual contributions must be clearly documented in the README file of
the GitHub repository.

Deliverables
The following deliverables must be submitted:
1. A project proposal document (PDF) including:
- Abstract (Include the project dataset link)
- Expected Contributions.

At the end you will submit a video explaining the project, a power point presentation
of the project and a project report (Not required for project proposal).

